#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / CA Certificates Specification
PACKAGE: ca-certificates
LANGUAGE: Data, shell/packaging integration
STATUS: W2
ROLE: System trust-anchor collection and trust-store construction

## PROGRAM
The CA certificate package supplies trusted certificate authorities and builds the system trust store used by supported applications.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream Ubuntu/Debian certificate package
BOUNDARY: certificate provenance -> package data -> trust-store generation -> application validation
WHITE_EDITION: provenance and update-process overlay

## SPEC
- trust anchors require explicit provenance
- no silent certificate additions/removals
- trust-store generation must be deterministic
- update failure must have a documented recovery path

## QUALITY
TEST: inventory, rebuild, TLS validation, invalid/expired/untrusted cases, upgrade, recovery
ECONOMY: trust-store size, rebuild time, startup impact

## SOURCE POLICY
Prefer packaging and update-process changes. Certificate-set changes require rationale, provenance, scope, and review date.
